    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0300" n="220" xml:id="pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">504.418A2/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Diekema</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-10T12:00:00-05:00">April 10,
                    1930—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>30. For Miller. Following telegram received from Doris Stevens: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“United States delegation Codification Conference making no effective
                            fight prevent adoption Nationality convention based on sex
                            discrimination. On contrary supporting two articles based on principle
                            inequality. Do you approve? If not urge send immediately precise
                            instructions Miller.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Please tell me what the two articles are as I would like to counteract unpleasant
                    publicity here. Certain women have been making most unfair criticisms which I
                    believe to be without any reason whatsoever.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
